INT. BOCA RATON CYBER LAB - NIGHT

= Alejandro monitors peer presence (tincan status) & pooled OpenRouter credits ($290) before receiving an emergency Kokoro TTS voice alert (tincan say) from Maya.

Rain streaks the glass of a darkened graduate research bay. Three monitors glow in Amber Phosphor CRT mode across ALEJANDRO's (20s, sharp, relentless) desk.

On the center display: TINCAN MESH OS v2.2. Floating windows pulse at READINESS TIER L3 (550 XP). A taut neon "tin-can string" vibrates between two pop-out windows across his dual monitors.

Alejandro's fingers fly across a mechanical keyboard.

ALEJANDRO
Let's see who's actually awake on the mesh.

He types `tincan status peer-secondary-node` and `tincan credits` into `win-terminal`.

The HUD flashes: `peer-secondary-node (Collaborator MacBook) — ONLINE. OpenRouter Pool: $290.00 across 4 Funded Labs.`

Suddenly, an incoming voice waveform ripples across his speaker bar. Local Kokoro-82M TTS synthesizes a crystal-clear voice in the room.

MAYA (V.O.)
(filtered, Kokoro TTS via `tincan say`)
Alejandro! Primary cloud ingress just went dark. Corporate SSO is locked out. Tell me the blind relay is up.

Alejandro smirks. He hits a hotkey.

ALEJANDRO
Zero accounts. Zero plaintext on the wire. Pin my key and hop into the Comms Studio.

INT. TORONTO LOFTS - CONTINUOUS

= During a cloud outage, Maya generates her zero-account Ed25519 identity (tincan whoami), pins Alejandro via TOFU (tincan add-contact), and initiates a WebRTC screen call (tincan call --screen).

!MAYA (20s, systems architect, hood up) sits in a candlelit loft during a grid brownout, tethered to a cellular hotspot.

She runs `tincan whoami` and `tincan add-contact alejandro`, pinning his Ed25519/X25519 identity via Trust-On-First-Use.

MAYA
Identity pinned. Opening sub-80ms UDP tunnel now.

She types: `tincan call alejandro --screen`.

INT. BOCA RATON CYBER LAB / INT. TORONTO LOFTS - INTERCUT

= Alejandro and Maya exchange X25519 sealed patches (tincan send/read), audit diffs via the AI Brain Arena, sync Watch Party telemetry (tincan playlist), and execute a HITL trigger (tincan actions/trigger) to ascend to L5.

On both of their screens, `Mesh Comms Studio.app` (`win-comms`) snaps open. Sub-80ms H.264 UDP video locks in.

Above the top HUD bar, a glowing cyan capsule arcs across the topology canvas. A synthesized WebAudio chord chimes: `+50 XP — FIRST HANDSHAKE (🟢 Mesh Initiate)`.

MAYA
(on WebRTC video)
I can see your second monitor pop-out! Look at the BroadcastChannel string tether pulsing between our windows.

ALEJANDRO
Send the zero-day patch payload through the Blind Relay. Even Railway can't decrypt the envelope—only my Curve25519 private key can open it.

Maya fires `tincan send alejandro "patch-v2.diff"` from her terminal.

On the background canvas of TinCan Mesh OS, a neon-blue X25519 capsule launches from `Collaborator MacBook`, slingshots through `Central Railway Relay`, and lands in Alejandro's mailbox (`+100 XP — 🥫 Cipher Postmaster`).

Alejandro runs `tincan read`. The ciphertext unseals locally (`+75 XP — 🔐 Zero-Knowledge Reader`).

MAYA
Wait—before we deploy the patch, which model should audit the assembly diff? Gemini 2.5 Pro or Claude Sonnet?

ALEJANDRO
Why guess? Let's run a blind Arena match.

Alejandro drags `AI Brain Router & Arena.app` (`win-arena`) to center screen, clicks the Quick Swap chip for `google/gemini-2.5-pro`, and hits Battle 2 Brains.

Two pink AI prompt packets streak from the relay to `gemini-brain` and `claude-brain`. Side-by-side diffs stream in real time. Maya's remote cyan cursor glides across Alejandro's screen and clicks Vote Winner (`+150 XP — 🧠 Synapse Arbiter`).

The top progress bar surges past `1,000 XP — TIER L4: CRDT GOSSIP & REAL-TIME WEBRTC MESH`.

MAYA
Now we need to trigger the remote hotfix on your workstation—hands-free while you keep monitoring the telemetry video feed.

In `Relay TV Watch Party.app` (`win-tv`), Alejandro clicks Sync Party and taps the `🔥` and `🥫` reaction buttons. Floating emoji particles rise across both of their monitors in lockstep (`+15 XP`).

Maya queues an inbound accessibility command from her terminal.

On Alejandro's screen, the Accessibility Gate (`tincan actions`) flashes amber: `[Action #1] From: maya — Execute production hotfix rollout (Pending Human-In-The-Loop Approval)`.

ALEJANDRO
Inbound action verified. Triggering now.

Alejandro types `tincan trigger 1` (`+200 XP — ⚡ HITL Commander`).

The HUD explodes into Messiah Gold as the room ascends to `TIER L5: AUTONOMOUS COGNITIVE MESH (2,000+ XP)`.

MAYA
(grinning)
Patched, verified, and zero keys exposed.

Alejandro leans back, typing `tincan screensaver`. The terminal dissolves into the animated half-block AI MESSIAH artwork pulsing peacefully in the dark.

>FADE OUT.
